{
  "slug": "dehumidifier-condensate-for-gardens",
  "capturedAt": "2026-06-01T15:21:52.583Z",
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A dehumidifier running 4 hours per day in a 40 m² basement extracts 2 to 5 litres of ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "distilled water",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termId": "cmpv463lb000018v4bpghekuv"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": " per day in summer. Over a month that is 60 to 150 litres. Using it in the garden rather than discarding it saves mains water and has some benefit in hard-water areas where alkaline mains water can raise soil pH over time.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What condensate contains",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Condensate is primarily distilled water with total dissolved solids typically below 50 ppm. Trace contaminants may include copper or aluminium from an old coil, trace organic compounds from the plastic housing. And biological content if the drip tray grows mould. A clean, well-serviced dehumidifier gives very low contamination. A dirty drip tray or mouldy coil raises the biological content.",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Safe uses",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Watering ornamental plants, shrubs, and trees: safe. Low mineral content is not a problem for established plants in soil.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Watering acid-loving plants in hard-water areas: beneficial. The low pH of condensate matches the preferred soil pH for these species and avoids the alkalinity of hard mains water.",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Topping up water butts: safe. Dilutes the collected rainwater and extends the water butt supply.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What to avoid",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Edible crops where water contacts the edible part: do not use condensate on leafy salads, herbs. Or soft fruit where the water touches what you eat. Use on the soil around the root zone only.",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Container plants with no soil reservoir: low TDS water used exclusively may slowly leach nutrients from potting mix. Mix with rainwater or supplement potting mix nutrients regularly.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Drinking or cooking: do not use condensate for food or drink. It is not safe to drink.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Storage",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Condensate stored more than 2 to 3 days develops bacterial growth, particularly in warm weather. Use promptly or add a few drops of ordinary household bleach per litre if storing for garden use. Do not store in the dehumidifier collection tank for more than 48 hours: empty the tank daily.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "title": "Troubleshooter"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Condensate has an unpleasant smell"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "The drip tray or collection tank has biological growth. Clean the tray with a dilute bleach solution, rinse well. And clean the dehumidifier coil with a soft brush. Condensate from a clean dehumidifier should be odourless.",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
